✅ Q7 — Find Duplicate Elements

🎗️ 7.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<Integer> containing positive, negative, and duplicate integers.
Using Java Streams, find all the elements that appear more than once in the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as a List<Integer>.
🔴 Preserve the original encounter order of the duplicate values.
🔴 Each duplicate value should appear only once in the result.
🔴 Correctly handle positive and negative integers.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Correctly handle a list containing no duplicates.

🎗️ 7.2 Input / Output

👉 Input : List<Integer> input = List.of(10, 25, 10, -5, 40, 25, 15, -5, 30, 25);
👉 Expected Output : [10, 25, -5]

🎗️ 7.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.
You can provide:

🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches you know
🔴 Your thoughts about empty-list behavior
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too